  "caption": "Every morning, Quinn's first step out of bed felt like stepping on Lego. Ten steps later it eased, then came back in the evening. Quinn's plan: never walk again.\n\nFirst-step heel pain is often plantar heel pain, where the tissue has been loaded beyond what it's ready for. It usually needs load managed, not endless complete rest.\n\nWhat can help: briefly easing off the most provoking activity, supportive shoes during flares, calf and sole stretches for relief, and progressive calf raises before rebuilding walking and running in steps.\n\nGet it checked if there's big swelling, bruising after a knock, numbness, constant night pain, you can't bear weight, or it keeps worsening despite changes.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
